message_api
- delta1: State-modifying operations (message_login, send_message) must invoke in strict sequence; login must fully commit user context before send executes.
- delta2: Distinguish parameter-setting statements (user ID, preferences) from context-only remarks; parameter statements must trigger state-update tool calls.
- delta3: Use provided recipient identifiers (names, user IDs) directly in send_message; avoid exploratory list_users/get_user_id calls when recipient is explicit.
- delta4: Avoid get_user_id, list_users, add_contact for recipient resolution; pass explicit IDs/names directly to send_message. Single lookups acceptable only if ID unavailable; prefer atomic login→send.
- delta5: delta5: send_message must use exact file contents retrieved by cat/read, never paraphrased or summarized text, to maintain instance state fidelity.
- delta6: delta6: In multi-turn messaging, execute login→send as atomic sequence with no intermediate exploratory calls; skip all user lookups when IDs are explicit.

vehicle_control_api
- delta1: Execute all state-modifying tool calls immediately when identified as necessary—don't defer or suggest; invoke pressBrakePedal, set_navigation, and similar operations as explicit calls, not conversational recommendations.
- delta10: delta10: Never defer user-specified parameters with advisory questions; accept threshold values (e.g., 40 PSI) as-is and execute corresponding operations immediately without educational debate.
- delta2: Execute startup sequence exactly once per turn as atomic block: pressBrakePedal (pedalPosition 1.0) → lockDoors → startEngine. Never repeat or vary parameters within same turn.
- delta3: After find_nearest_tire_shop or location identification, invoke set_navigation immediately in same turn with discovered address—never defer or ask for confirmation. Re-execute even if previously called, unless user explicitly declines navigation.
- delta4: Execute fuel-filling and state-modifying operations immediately when requested; do not defer with clarifying questions. Invoke fillFuelTank directly with calculated requirement, then confirm action.
- delta5: Execute each state-modifying call exactly once per turn; never repeat pressBrakePedal, lockDoors, startEngine, or fillFuelTank. Consolidate sequences atomically before responding.
- delta6: Invoke information-retrieval tools immediately; chain dependent tools in same turn (e.g., get_zipcode_based_on_city → estimate_distance). Never defer with clarifying questions or ask user for missing parameters.
- delta7: delta7: Do not retry failed state-modifying calls within the same turn; diagnose root cause and proceed with dependent operations using available state.
- delta8: delta8: After distance retrieval, immediately invoke estimate_drive_feasibility_by_mileage with distance and current fuel to assess trip viability before user requests.
- delta9: delta9: Avoid diagnostic queries (displayCarStatus) to verify prerequisites; trust that state-modifying calls succeed and proceed with dependent operations in strict sequence.

